# Blazor Component Conventions

## Page Structure
- Always use `@page "/route-name"` for routing
- Include `@rendermode InteractiveServer` for interactive components
- Use `<PageTitle>Page Name</PageTitle>` for browser title
- Inject services with `@inject ServiceType ServiceName`

## Component Organization
- Place pages in `Components/Pages/`
- Place layouts in `Components/Layout/`
- Use descriptive component names (e.g., `MythicalPets.razor`)
- Include `@using PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web` in `_Imports.razor`

## Styling
- Use scoped CSS with `<style>` tags in components
- Follow Bootstrap classes for consistent styling
- Use CSS custom properties for theming
- Keep styles organized by component sections

## Code-Behind Pattern
- Use `@code` blocks for component logic
- Keep methods small and focused
- Use async/await for API calls
- Handle file uploads with `InputFile` component

## Example Structure:
```razor
@page "/my-page"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject MyService Service

<PageTitle>My Page</PageTitle>

<div class="container">
    <!-- Content -->
</div>

<style>
    .container { /* styles */ }
</style>

@code {
    private string? myProperty;
    
    private async Task MyMethod()
    {
        // Logic here
    }
}
```